# Wayfarer's Rest is protected against non-op players (life/mortal_spawn.js, KubeJS: no FTB Chunks claim exists in the Mortal
# Realm, claims are Life-2-only). `ttl wayfarer expect <player> <x> <dy> <z> protected|open` asks the function the break and
# place events use; dy is relative to the plaza feet (plaza floor = -1), x/z are Mortal Realm coordinates (bell roof at 0 0).
# Needs the spawn placed (`ttl spawn` prints it). The real events and explosions are on the "verify in game" list: bots do not break blocks.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWayfarer
@sleep 2
# the plaza, under the bell roof, the shrine side: refused
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 0 -1 5 protected
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 0 -1 0 protected
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 0 3 0 protected
# beyond the 39 x 39 box, far above the 22 blocks of height, below the foundations, an empty corner column: free
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 60 -1 5 open
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 0 40 5 open
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 0 -12 5 open
ttl wayfarer expect TtlBotWayfarer 24 -1 -14 open
ttlbot remove TtlBotWayfarer
